Subject: [PATCH] c6x: avoid call debug labels inside execute packets

With -g and var-tracking, dwarf2out emits a label for
DW_AT_call_return_pc right after every call that carries a
REG_CALL_ARG_LOCATION note.  c6x puts calls first in their execute
packet, so the label lands between the call and the parallel insns:

	callp	.s2	(consume_seq), B3
  .LVL9:
  ||	mv	.l1x	B4, A4

and gas fails with "label not at start of execute packet".  This
breaks libgcc's shared build (hardcfr.c is compiled with -g).

c6x runs var-tracking itself in c6x_reorg, before the bundles are
formed, so drop the call site note from calls that share a packet with
other insns when building the bundle.  Only call site debug info for
those calls is lost; code generation is unchanged.

The bundled calls can carry the REG_CALL_ARG_LOCATION note more than
once (seen with callp in hardcfr.c), so all of them must be removed.

---
 gcc/config/c6x/c6x.cc | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

--- a/gcc/config/c6x/c6x.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/c6x/c6x.cc
@@ -4589,6 +4589,23 @@
   rtx_insn *t;
   int i;
 
+  /* With var-tracking, the debug back end emits a label for
+     DW_AT_call_return_pc right after any call carrying a
+     REG_CALL_ARG_LOCATION note.  If the call shares its execute packet
+     with other insns, that label would end up in the middle of the
+     packet, which the assembler rejects.  Drop the call site
+     information for such calls.  A call can carry more than one such
+     note, so remove all of them.  */
+  if (n_filled > 1)
+    for (i = 0; i < n_filled; i++)
+      if (CALL_P (slot[i]))
+	{
+	  rtx note;
+	  while ((note = find_reg_note (slot[i], REG_CALL_ARG_LOCATION,
+					NULL_RTX)) != NULL_RTX)
+	    remove_note (slot[i], note);
+	}
+
   seq = gen_rtx_SEQUENCE (VOIDmode, gen_rtvec_v (n_filled, slot));
   bundle = make_insn_raw (seq);
   BLOCK_FOR_INSN (bundle) = BLOCK_FOR_INSN (slot[0]);
